+// nothing but the mark is in the crop.
+// KEYED ON `SIX_ARM`, and read at EVERY count the design names, 6 to 16 (LAWS P6 §E: pass 6 read
+// six alone, and arm (c)'s clause was false at six of the ten later steps):
+//   (a) title / (b) heading — the FLOOR: every written count out-weighs one graphite stroke.
+//       Plant: a rung the floor must see as lighter than one, at six AND at seven (the thinnest
+//       numeral: ×1.19 of one against six's ×1.41). In light that is the rung below title
+//       (heading); in dark the heading rung clears one stroke, so the dark plant is the body rung.
+//       Arm (b) is RED in light by design: that is its ballot price.
+//   (c) remainder — every count from six paints at least 6/5 of five strokes' ink. It does NOT
+//       promise the ink grows with the room: a written number is not monotone in its value, and
+//       the table printed here is the ballot's (ink and ink per person at every count). Plant: the
+//       remainder and its plus hidden, read at every count, must fall under the bar.
+const G16_PLANT = (theme: "light" | "dark"): string =>
+  SIX_ARM === "remainder"
+    ? ".pt-count.is-rest, .pt-plus { visibility: hidden !important; }"
